<title>FINLAND: ASKO SELLS FUTURUM STOCK TO TRANSFORMA.</title>
<headline>ASKO SELLS FUTURUM STOCK TO TRANSFORMA.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1996-12-16</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish plastic pipe, furniture and white goods maker Asko Oy said in a statement on Monday its Swedish subsidiary Asko AB will sell its shares in Futurum AB to Transforma Invest AB.</p>
<p>Skelleftea-based Futurum is a maker of kitchen stove fans. The unit's annual net sales are around 130 million Swedish crowns.</p>
<p>The divestment is part of Asko's Kodinkone white goods arm's strategy to focus on the manufacturing and marketing of big household appliances, Asko said.</p>
<p>--Helsinki Newsroom  +358 - 9 - 680 50 245</p>
